  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Arizona recorded $143M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Arizona awarded 921 contracts in the period, with an average award size of $155K. Arizona obligations are down 99.6% year over year. Arizona fiscal history shows much larger totals in recent completed years: FY22 totaled $16.4B, FY23 totaled $20.9B, FY24 totaled $19.3B, FY25 totaled $25.6B, and FY26 totaled $34.7B. Arizona top buyers for FY2027 to date are led by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $94.6M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $13.9M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $12M. Arizona top vendors for FY2027 to date include JACOBS ENGINEERING GROUP INC. with $13.7M and FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. with $13.5M. Arizona largest industries by obligation in FY2027 to date include Engineering Services at $14M and All Other Business Support Services at $13.7M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "Arizona FY2027 to date obligations totaled $143M, compared with past-year totals of $16.4B in FY22, $20.9B in FY23, $19.3B in FY24, $25.6B in FY25, and $34.7B in FY26. Arizona obligations are down 99.6% year over year. Arizona award count in FY2027 to date was 921 with an average award size of $155K. Arizona current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors drove FY2027 to date spending in Arizona?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $94.6M in Arizona, making it the largest buyer for FY2027 to date. The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $13.9M and $12M respectively. JACOBS ENGINEERING GROUP INC. and FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. are the top vendors, with obligations of $13.7M and $13.5M respectively."
      }
    ]
